siren_test.description:
⚠️ **Real sirens sound here** – one at a time, short, with confirmation before each sound.

Requirements (checked by the siren guard): all areas disarmed, hardware enabled, **test mode off**, no smoke detector active, burglar tones only. Arming is blocked during the test; disarming cancels it.

Last tested: {last}

siren_tone_edit.description:
Tones reported by this siren: {tones}

The chosen tone is used in an alarm and in the siren test. Afterwards, best run a short, quiet siren test.

**Fire tones** (with “fire”, “smoke” or “Brand” in the name) are locked for burglar alarms: people who hear a fire tone leave the house – possibly right towards the intruder – and a fire tone that also sounds for burglary is taken less seriously in a real fire. Only if the name is misleading (e.g. the only loud tone of an outdoor siren is called “fire”) can experts release it. Never for smoke detectors with a siren. The fire lock always applies.

